scenario: known_sources
Known sources, for one key and for every key, of each kind. A known CIDR silences the whole request, even new in every way. A known country, ASN or client silences only a new place of its own kind, so each step below is new in just the one way its source covers and raises nothing, and the last step of each key, which no source covers, raises. The Oslo office is a source of the key other only, so the same country used on app still raises.

